    "done_when": "First reproduce at main: the case fails with the watch thread raising TypeError for the unexpected changed_at keyword (the log at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261001T010414677018-changes-push-rows/logs/base-gate.log shows it). Then the spy accepts and forwards the same arguments the real function takes, so the case passes and still fails if the watch stops calling the invalidation; add an assertion that the watch passed a changed_at stamp, since the change-time guard depends on it. Only that test file changes; no source file changes. The named negative control (the watch stops calling the invalidation, patched in memory inside the test process, never on disk) reddens the case, and its log records that the patch applied. The gate is tests/test_metadata_index_survives_restart.py, tests/test_page_paints_from_the_index.py and tests/test_changes_push_rows.py at base and at head. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder; each log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. Every pytest process uses a basetemp private to that process. The head arm adds no failure id and removes the one named above. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed path report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
